# Runway — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in. Every variable the application reads
# MUST be listed here, with placeholders only — never a real key, ever.
#
# Names follow Nuxt's runtimeConfig binding: NUXT_PUBLIC_* fills
# `runtimeConfig.public.*`, NUXT_* fills the server-only section. Nothing in
# nuxt.config.ts reads process.env, so these resolve at RUNTIME — which is what
# lets Netlify change them without a rebuild.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — public. These reach the browser, which is expected and safe: the
# anon/publishable key is a public identifier, and Row Level Security is what
# actually protects the data. See docs/database/rls.md.
#
# The anon key may be either a legacy JWT (eyJ...) or a new publishable key
# (sb_publishable_...). Both work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NUXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NUXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — server only. NEVER prefix this with NUXT_PUBLIC_ and never move it
# into runtimeConfig.public. The service-role key has BYPASSRLS: it ignores every
# policy in docs/database/rls.md. No code reads it yet; it is declared so the
# boundary exists before something needs it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NUXT_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-or-secret-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development needs none of the above. `supabase start` prints its own URL
# and keys, and `bun run test:rls` reads them from `supabase status` directly —
# they are never hardcoded. See docs/database/local-development.md.
#
# Do NOT put SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN or SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD in .env. Linking this
# repo to the hosted project is a deliberate human act, not an ambient default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
